@mhevery hm, just noticed
> The reason we remove the unknown elements

but the problem is not with the elements removing, this has not changed in that update, the problem is with inner text removing

> The reason we remove the unknown elements is that they could be web-components which would allow user to trigger code, and could provide security hole.

@mhevery, I don't understand. The old behavior was to keep the safe content (so unknown custom elements would still be stripped of, but their safe content such as text nodes would be retained). There was a problem with comment nodes being converted to text nodes (#26007), but that could have been fixed in a non-breaking way, I guess.

I don't understand what security implications this change had 😕
